<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liu Zhiyuan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">895–948</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Emperor Gaozu of Later Han</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liu Zhiyuan was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shatuo">Shatuo</a> general who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiyuan">Taiyuan</a> under the Later Jin. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Khitan Liao</a> army took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a> in 947 and ended that dynasty, he proclaimed himself emperor, and as the Khitan withdrew he entered Kaifeng and founded the Later Han, the shortest of the Five Dynasties. He died early in 948 and was succeeded by his young son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-chengyou">Liu Chengyou</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liu-zhiyuan.jpg" alt="Liu Zhiyuan" width="300" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 王圻 王思義輯 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%BE%8C%E6%BC%A2%E9%AB%98%E7%A5%96%E5%83%8F.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
